WEBVTT

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.150
In my opinion, Wake Up, Girls! 
doesn't need Hayashida Airi.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.190
As you all know,

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:43.290
I am currently responsible 
for managing Wake Up, Girls!.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:44.660
Let me cut to the chase.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.960
I'm thinking of cutting 
Hayashida Airi from the group.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.460
Hold on! You can't just...

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.800
I just told you.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.720
You're currently under my control.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:57.460
If you're willing to cut 
Hayashida Airi now,

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:59.220
I will continue your lessons.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.180
If you can't, you're all fired.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:07.730
Give me your decision in ten minutes.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.740
Why did you say that?!

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.170
I simply cast a stone.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:29.120
What? I'm not interested 
in discussing Zen riddles with you!

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.880
Neither am I.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.040
Considering you work with I-1,

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.870
it's no wonder you think 
Wake Up, Girls! is terrible.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.130
They're hardly professionals,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.910
but they're working through 
it at their own pace.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:52.670
If you shake them now when their 
teamwork isn't solid yet, they...

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.650
If that's all it takes to crush them, 
they're not good enough.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.780
President!

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.290
Lions push their cubs 
off cliffs and raise

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.030
only those who climb back up.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.270
Those who can't climb back up 
the cliff can't survive in the jungle.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:13.740
But don't expect me to say 
something so hot-blooded.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:23.030
Potatoes can't come climbing back 
up if you roll them down a hill.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.050
President!

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:28.430
Say something!

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.560
What should we do?

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.540
There's nothing we can do.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.780
Huh? Are you saying 
we should cut Ai-chan?

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.070
That's not what I said.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.820
What should we do, leader?

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:46.760
What?

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.260
We only have seven minutes left.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:56.890
Should we take a vote?

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:58.680
Without even talking about it?

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:03.410
But time keeps passing 
while we talk about it.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.720
Yoppi!

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.850
Stop forcing me 
to make every decision!

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:11.480
Huh? But you're our leader...

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:15.730
Yeah, but why do I 
have to make the decision?

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:18.500
We're not asking you to do that.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.390
We won't get anywhere like this.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:24.350
We're running out of time!

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:25.990
You shut up.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:27.440
But...

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:28.850
What should I do, then?!

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.620
Should I decide if we're voting or not?!

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.040
It's not like that.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.050
Honestly speaking, I don't 
think you have any talent.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.340
Why are you having fun?

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.330
It's almost time.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:23.340
I want Airi to stay.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:28.470
Does that mean you're okay 
with everyone being fired?

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:29.810
What?!

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:32.710
Are you saying you'd cut her?

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:40.110
This must be the difference 
between us and I-1.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:41.420
What do you mean?

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:46.170
We're not sure if we're just 
playing with our friends or not.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.610
I don't get it.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.730
Because we get upset so easily,

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.100
we'll be treated like amateurs forever!

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.060
Treated like amateurs?

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.460
Isn't it true, though?

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.850
That's why people 
say Wake Up, Girls!

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:01.720
doesn't exist without Shimada Mayu!

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.250
You're bringing that up now?

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:08.310
After all, we're not 
here to make friends.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:10.560
We're here to become idols.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.640
Yoppi's right.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:19.100
I'm sick of fighting like this!

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.950
I quit.

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:24.200
I wanted to go to Hikarizuka 
in the first place.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.070
I was just doing this 
to improve my skills until then.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.920
What? This was just 
a stepping stone for you?

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:33.830
Your dream or delusion 
has nothing to do with this.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.860
What are you calling a delusion?

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:37.280
Don't call it that!

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.460
We're getting off track.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:41.080
Stop!

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:41.960
What?

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.970
I'm so hungry!

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:48.830
Minami.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:55.010
Here.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:01.850
Yoppi.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:07.110
I'm not sure how to put this, 
but is that what we're doing?

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:08.490
What?

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:12.860
You're right that we're 
here to become idols,

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:15.630
but is that what being 
an idol is about?

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:21.580
I don't think it's 
Wake Up, Girls! without Airi.

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.000
Yeah.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:26.220
Even the president said the

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.510
seven of us together 
make Wake Up, Girls!.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.710
You're right.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:34.640
When I ran away, 
Airi came to get me.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:36.600
I'll bring her back.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.640
I'll bring Airi back.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:42.570
I'll go with you.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:43.450
So will I.

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:45.130
I'll go, too.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:46.290
Me, too.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.020
No, I'll go.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:49.780
After all, I'm the leader.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:51.110
Mayushi.

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:59.320
This is our decision, right?

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:00.340
What?

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:03.340
We're not abandoning Airi.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:04.290
Yes.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.610
Don't you think we're 
being messed with?

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:09.930
I feel like we're being 
thrown out of order.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:14.790
Besides, he has no right to fire us.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:19.830
But even the president said 
he had total control over us.

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.390
Then let's try talking 
to the president.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:23.690
Yeah.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.690
<b>Next Stop: Kita-Yobancho</b>

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.680
I can't believe Ai-chan skipped 
practice without saying anything.

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:31.260
Yeah.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.810
Hayasaka-san must have 
been pretty hard on her.

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:35.450
Probably.

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:39.970
You waited for her 
that day, didn't you?

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:41.450
Have you heard anything?

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.510
She didn't tell me anything.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:47.210
She didn't tell you, huh?

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:51.010
I understand how that feels.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:51.720
Huh?

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:55.970
The next stop is Kita-Yobancho.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.510
I heard.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.200
Then you understand 
what's wrong with

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:05.140
what Hayasaka-san is saying, right?

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.730
What's so wrong about it?

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:11.050
We belong to Green Leaves, don't we?

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:15.580
You're the only one who 
can decide if we're fired.

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:18.120
Didn't I tell you?

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:21.120
I'm leaving it up to 
Hayasaka-san this time.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:23.940
I knew this would happen.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:28.250
But we want to keep working 
as a group of seven with Airi.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.810
You can't smoke in here.

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.840
Aren't you talking 
to the wrong person?

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:36.510
What?

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:39.240
Go confront Hayasaka-san.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.660
So that's your answer.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:42.270
This is getting crazy.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:43.410
I understand.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:46.020
Where is he?

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:48.020
<b>Kumagaiya</b>

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:56.030
What do you want?

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.780
Huh? I thought I'd help out.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:02.910
What brings you here?

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:07.140
Huh? The daughter 
of a confectioner doesn't need

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:08.790
a reason to make sweets.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:12.900
So this is how you make them.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:13.800
You're in the way.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.150
Isn't there anything I can do to help?

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.280
No.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:21.300
Don't you have your thing today?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.230
What?

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:24.930
You're always going to your lessons.

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:29.060
Go line up those sweets.

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:31.820
Okay.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:35.570
Huh?

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:39.660
Airi, you're helping around 
the shop? How unusual.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:40.290
Yeah.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:42.090
You must be so happy, Dad.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:47.330
<b>Mori no Miyako Game Land</b>

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.650
Is he really here?

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.340
Matsuda-san doesn't lie.

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:56.340
There he is!

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:04.170
You won't cut Hayashida Airi, 
but you want to continue your lessons?

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:09.930
Don't you think you're pushing your luck?

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:10.980
You're right.

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:14.410
But this is the conclusion we 
reached after discussing it together.

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:18.530
Even the president 
told us to come talk to you.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:21.740
I see.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:25.980
You can start by doing 
what I tell you to do.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:27.220
All right!

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:29.710
It's still too early to celebrate.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.870
Could you go get 
three of those for me?

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:41.220
Airi...

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:44.210
Well? Don't I look good?

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:48.930
Okay, just like that.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.630
That was close.

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:51.640
We'll get it next time.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:56.180
You've been saying "we'll get it 
next time" since three tries ago.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.310
Shut up!

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:58.570
Stop, stop!

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:01.070
You're too slow!

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.900
I told you to shut up!

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:09.180
Um...

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:11.660
Here you go.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.790
Sorry all we ever 
have is our sweets.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.550
Oh, Airi made these.

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:22.300
That's why they look a little funny.

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:25.020
That's enough, Mom.

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.300
Okay, okay. I'm sorry 
for bothering you.

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:32.260
Listen...

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:35.310
I'm thinking of quitting WUG.

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:41.070
Unlike everyone else, 
I don't have any talent.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.550
Even if I keep practicing, I...

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:49.330
Did Hayasaka-san tell you that?

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:50.830
Yeah.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:02.590
You're not having any luck.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:04.840
What are you going to do?

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:08.730
I'm going to get more change.

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:14.310
I'll give it a try.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.350
What?

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:21.560
I thought I could get somewhere 
with enough practice, but I can't.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.030
I feel the same way about myself.

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:28.110
You and I are on different levels.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.350
I love Wake Up, Girls!.

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:38.500
When I'm with everyone, 
I can't help how much fun I'm having.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:46.630
Since the audition, I've always 
thought everyone's so cute.

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:49.640
I felt elated.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:59.320
I wrongly assumed just being with 
you made me part of the group.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:00.270
Wrongly assumed?

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:02.780
Yeah, I was wrong.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:04.710
Now that I think about it,

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:09.490
there's something wrong with 
me being in the same group

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:15.290
as a former I-1 center and 
someone who's been in magazines.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.780
I don't think that's true.

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:18.710
It is.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:19.370
What?

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.540
It is true.

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:25.670
After all, I'm the only 
one who's different.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:26.380
What?

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.930
I'm the only one with no presence.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:31.630
That's not...

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:33.350
You don't need to force yourself, Yoppi.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.180
I'm not forcing anything.

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:38.940
I understand who I am.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:41.560
Why would you say that?

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:49.030
I decided to join WUG and try being 
an idol again because of you.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:49.820
What?

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:55.630
When I heard you were auditioning 
and we sang and danced together,

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:57.080
I realized something.

00:14:57.510 --> 00:15:01.080
I like doing this kind of thing.

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:07.280
Because the night is cold, tomorrow...

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:09.340
The mic is bothering me, 
and I can't sing!

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.670
Let me see that.

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:14.800
Remember this distance between 
your mouth and the mic.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:16.190
Huh.

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:17.480
Give it a try.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:29.200
<i>When I was depressed, 
you appeared blindingly bright.</i>

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:42.000
You were shining then.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:45.750
That's how it looked to me.

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:50.070
You made me decide to return.

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:54.490
So don't say you're quitting.

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:58.100
You've got it!

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.140
You can do it!

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:02.640
Just like that!

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:04.400
All right!

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:07.200
I got one! Okay, let's get another!

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.020
Let's keep up our energy!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.630
Yeah!

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:18.870
I'm sorry. I can't do it.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:22.200
I may have been shining then,

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:25.880
but now I'm just 
holding everyone back.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.960
So, what?

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:28.750
Huh?

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:31.010
Then let's make sure you don't!

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:34.330
I'll even help you!

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:38.190
At the very least, 
it's not too late to quit until...

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.600
until after you've tried everything!

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:43.880
Yoppi...

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:49.260
I don't know how 
I ended up as our leader,

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.900
but I have no idea 
what I'm supposed to do!

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:57.460
I don't know what I'm doing.

00:16:57.460 --> 00:17:01.100
Everyone keeps telling me things, 
and they seem really worried.

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.770
I even tried organizing 
everyone's thoughts,

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:06.790
but I couldn't even organize my own.

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:11.140
When Hayasaka-san told us 
to decide whether we'd continue

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:14.940
our lessons or cut you 
from the group...

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:17.930
everyone kept saying 
leader, leader, but...

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.380
So that's what happened.

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:19.930
What?

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:24.620
Don't worry about me anymore.

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:26.810
I don't want to cause 
any more trouble.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.690
You said we shouldn't 
worry on our own!

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:33.240
You're the one who said 
we shouldn't worry on our own.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.780
Worry with the rest of us, then.

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:37.150
Let's think together.

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:40.700
If we don't do that, 
what's the purpose of this group?

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:42.890
You can talk to us about anything.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:46.210
We're a group. Let's come 
up with something together.

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:51.930
You're amazing, Minami!

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:53.640
Airi! Airi!

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:55.420
Airi! Airi!

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:57.090
Airi! Airi!

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:58.290
Airi!

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:00.420
Your time's almost up.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:04.020
Hayasaka-san, 
give us one more chance.

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:07.350
Prepare yourself, Musubimaru!

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:14.100
After discussing it, we decided 
we'd do anything to bring you back!

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:17.590
That's why Mayushi and I came here!

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:22.870
This is my first command as a leader.

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:26.120
Come back, Airi!

00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:59.400
All right!

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:02.630
Yes, yes!

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:04.190
Yeah!

00:19:05.530 --> 00:19:06.360
Here.

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:18.170
Thank you.

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:19.920
It's okay.

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:22.430
Why are you crying, Yoppi?

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:23.850
I don't know.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:30.940
<b>Sender: Kikuma Kaya</b>

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:30.940
<b>Subject: All right!</b>

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.430
<i>Hayasaka has fallen.</i>

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:30.940
<i>How are you guys doing?</i>

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:32.640
Fallen?

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:37.190
<b>To: Kikuma Kaya</b>

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:37.190
<b>Subject: Re: All right!</b>

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.190
<i>We're on our way with Airi.</i>

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:47.200
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:47.200
What?

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:50.610
They completed their Musubimaru task, 
so you changed your mind?

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:53.080
Airi's staying on board?

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:55.590
Can't you explain so I'll understand?

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:58.870
What did Hayasaka-san say?

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:02.470
As usual, I had no idea 
what he was saying...

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:05.670
In any case, Airi has returned to WUG,

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:09.210
and he's going to 
continue his lessons.

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:10.390
Really?

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:16.320
He says he's sick of watching 
amateur potatoes pretend to be friends,

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:21.020
but it seems that's what 
that weirdo likes about them.

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:21.740
What?

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:26.410
It must be because he's 
worked with I-1 for so long.

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:32.370
Dad.

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:37.630
I know I'm in the middle of helping you, 
but something came up.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.450
See you later.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.700
Persistence pays off.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:45.390
Huh?

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:50.270
I'm saying you can't 
give up on everything.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:53.770
Go do it.

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:56.520
See you later.

00:20:58.620 --> 00:20:59.770
I'm sorry.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.470
Ai-chan...

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:02.400
Sheesh.

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:08.840
Welcome back.

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.090
I finally got to say 
what I wanted to say.

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:16.750
Huh?

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:19.990
I think I understand what 
Karina-san meant when

00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:22.040
she said we should fight.

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:23.340
Yeah.

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:29.560
Mayushi, if there's anything 
you want to say...

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:38.830
Excuse me...

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:39.360
Huh?

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:45.740
I-I'll make you 
acknowledge me someday.

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:50.440
My acknowledgment 
won't do you any good.

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:55.460
You need ordinary people 
to recognize you.

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:57.870
In other words, your audience.

00:21:57.870 --> 00:21:59.630
Anyway, here.

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:08.650
It's an application form 
for the idol festival.

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:10.760
<b>"Idol Festival" 2014</b>

00:22:08.650 --> 00:22:10.760
You will be entering this.

00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:13.260
What?!

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:14.970
To be continued

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:47.500
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:45.380 --> 00:23:47.830
Mayushi, are you friends with Yoppi?

00:23:47.830 --> 00:23:49.100
Huh? Where did that come from?

00:23:49.100 --> 00:23:51.740
It just always seems that way.

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:53.030
You think so?

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:53.930
We're just ordinary friends.

00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:56.040
I see. That's fine, then.

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:57.720
What? That sounded 
really significant...

00:23:57.720 --> 00:24:00.250
The next episode is "Commotion"!

00:23:57.720 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"Commotion"</b>
